/-!
# The system of quotients of a directed system of étale equivalence relations

The proof of Stacks 07SU produces a directed inverse system of étale equivalence relations
`R_i ⇉ V_i` of objects of the big fppf site of `S` whose squares

```
R_i  ⟶ R_{i'}
 ↓s_i    ↓s_{i'}
V_i  ⟶ V_{i'}
```

are cartesian (Stacks 07SV), and passes to the system of quotients `X_i = V_i / R_i`. It then
records of that system: every `X_i` is an algebraic space, quasi-separated and of finite type
over `Spec ℤ` (Stacks 07S4, 040W, 040Y); there are transition maps `X_i ⟶ X_{i'}`; the squares
formed by `V_i ⟶ V_{i'}`, the quotient maps and `X_i ⟶ X_{i'}` are cartesian (Stacks 07S3);
and therefore `X_i ⟶ X_{i'}` is affine as soon as `V_i ⟶ V_{i'}` is (Stacks 03WG).

This file establishes these facts for an arbitrary directed system of étale equivalence
relations with cartesian source squares.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.relationQuotient` — the quotient sheaf `U/R` of the étale equivalence
  relation given by `s, t : R ⟶ U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.relationQuotientSystem` — the inverse system `j ↦ V_j / R_j` of
  quotients of a system of relations `s, t : R ⟶ V`, with transition maps induced on quotient
  sheaves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.quotientSystemπ` — the natural transformation `h_{V_j} ⟶ V_j/R_j`
  formed by the quotient maps.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_quotientSystem_obj`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.quotientSystemπ_app_surjective`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.quotientSystemπ_app_etale` — every stage is an algebraic space,
  charted by a surjective étale quotient map (Stacks 02WW).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isPullback_quotientSystemπ` — the chart squares of the system are
  cartesian (Stacks 07S3).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAffineHom_quotientSystem_map` — the transition maps are affine
  when those of `V` are (Stacks 03WG).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_quotient_of_quasiCompact_source` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_quotientSystem_obj` — a quotient is
  quasi-separated when the presenting scheme is and the source map is quasi-compact
  (Stacks 07S4).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_of_chart` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_quotientSystem_obj` — a presheaf with a
  surjective étale chart whose source is quasi-compact and locally of finite type over the
  integers is of finite type over `Spec ℤ` (Stacks 040Y, 073B).
* `CategoryTheory.Limits.isPullback_limit_π_limMap` — over a cofiltered index category, a
  natural transformation all of whose naturality squares are cartesian has cartesian squares
  `lim F ⟶ F j` over `lim G ⟶ G j`.

## Implementation notes

*The transition maps.* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap` is the map of quotient sheaves
induced by a morphism of pre-relations, and depends only on the map of base objects
(`Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq`); functoriality of the system is therefore
`Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_id` and `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_comp`.

*The chart squares.* Stacks 07S3 is `Stacks.Groupoids.isPullback_toQuotientSheaf`, stated for
the projection `points F U ⟶ U/R` out of the restricted functor of points. The quotient map
`h_U ⟶ U/R` of Stacks 02WW is that projection precomposed with the comparison
`Stacks.Groupoids.yonedaToPoints`, an isomorphism because `Over.post B.inclusion` is fully
faithful, so the square transports along the comparison.

*Affine transitions.* Stacks 03WG, implication (4) ⇒ (2), at the surjective étale chart
`h_{V_{j'}} ⟶ X_{j'}`: the base change of `X_j ⟶ X_{j'}` along it is `h_{V_j} ⟶ h_{V_{j'}}`
by the chart square, and that is affine by (1) ⇒ (2) for representable presheaves.

*Quasi-separation.* Stacks 07S4 asks for quasi-compactness of one projection of the kernel
pair of the chart; the kernel pair of the quotient map is the relation itself (Stacks 02WV,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.quotientMap_isPullback`), so the hypothesis is quasi-compactness of
the scheme morphism underlying `s`.

*Finite type over `Spec ℤ`.* A chart over `S` becomes a chart of the view over `Spec ℤ` by
`CategoryTheory.OverShriek.relocalizePresheafFunctor`, corrected by the comparison
`Λ h_U ≅ h_{j U}` of Stacks 03I4 part (2); local finite type is then Stacks 040Y, conditions
(1) and (6), and quasi-compactness is Stacks 073B part (1) against the terminal presheaf, which
is quasi-separated.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07S3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07S3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07S4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07S4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02WW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02WW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03WG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03WG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 040Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/040Y)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.OverShriek Opposite

universe u

/-! ### Cartesian naturality squares pass to cofiltered limits -/

namespace CategoryTheory.Limits

/-- **Cartesian naturality squares pass to the limit.** Let `q : F ⟶ G` be a natural
transformation of diagrams indexed by a cofiltered category, all of whose naturality squares
are cartesian. Then for every index `j` the square formed by the projections
`lim F ⟶ F j`, `lim G ⟶ G j`, the limit map `lim F ⟶ lim G` and `q j` is cartesian.

Given a cone over the cospan, its components at the stages over `j` are the lifts through the
cartesian squares at the maps `k ⟶ j`; these form a cone over `F` restricted to `Over j`, and
the restriction of the limit cone of `F` is still limiting because `Over j ⥤ I` is initial. -/
theorem isPullback_limit_π_limMap {I C : Type*} [Category* I] [Category* C]
    [IsCofilteredOrEmpty I] {F G : I ⥤ C} [HasLimit F] [HasLimit G] (q : F ⟶ G)
    (hq : ∀ ⦃i i' : I⦄ (f : i ⟶ i'), IsPullback (F.map f) (q.app i) (q.app i') (G.map f))
    (j : I) :
    IsPullback (limit.π F j) (limMap q) (q.app j) (limit.π G j) := by
  have hc : IsLimit ((limit.cone F).whisker (Over.forget j)) :=
    (Functor.Initial.isLimitWhiskerEquiv (Over.forget j) _).symm (limit.isLimit F)
  let x (s : PullbackCone (q.app j) (limit.π G j)) (k : Over j) : s.pt ⟶ F.obj k.left :=
    (hq k.hom).lift s.fst (s.snd ≫ limit.π G k.left) (by
      rw [Category.assoc, limit.w]
      exact s.condition)
  let cs (s : PullbackCone (q.app j) (limit.π G j)) : Cone (Over.forget j ⋙ F) :=
    { pt := s.pt
      π :=
        { app := fun k => x s k
          naturality := by
            intro k k' m
            dsimp
            rw [Category.id_comp]
            apply (hq k'.hom).hom_ext
            · rw [Category.assoc, ← F.map_comp, Over.w m, IsPullback.lift_fst,
                IsPullback.lift_fst]
            · rw [Category.assoc, q.naturality, IsPullback.lift_snd_assoc, IsPullback.lift_snd,
                Category.assoc, limit.w] } }
  have hfac (s : PullbackCone (q.app j) (limit.π G j)) (k : Over j) :
      hc.lift (cs s) ≫ limit.π F k.left = x s k :=
    hc.fac (cs s) k
  refine IsPullback.of_isLimit' ⟨by simp⟩ (PullbackCone.IsLimit.mk _ (fun s => hc.lift (cs s))
    ?_ ?_ ?_)
  · intro s
    have h' : x s (Over.mk (𝟙 j)) ≫ F.map (𝟙 j) = s.fst := (hq (𝟙 j)).lift_fst _ _ _
    have h'' : (hc.lift (cs s) ≫ limit.π F j) ≫ F.map (𝟙 j) = s.fst :=
      (congrArg (· ≫ F.map (𝟙 j)) (hfac s (Over.mk (𝟙 j)))).trans h'
    simpa using h''
  · intro s
    apply limit.hom_ext
    intro i
    obtain ⟨k, a, b, -⟩ := IsCofilteredOrEmpty.cone_objs i j
    have hk : hc.lift (cs s) ≫ limit.π F k = x s (Over.mk b) := hfac s (Over.mk b)
    rw [Category.assoc, limMap_π, ← limit.w F a, Category.assoc, q.naturality,
      ← Category.assoc, hk, ← Category.assoc]
    change ((hq b).lift s.fst (s.snd ≫ limit.π G k) _ ≫ q.app k) ≫ G.map a =
      s.snd ≫ limit.π G i
    rw [IsPullback.lift_snd, Category.assoc, limit.w]
  · intro s m hm₁ hm₂
    apply hc.hom_ext
    intro k
    change m ≫ limit.π F k.left = hc.lift (cs s) ≫ limit.π F k.left
    rw [hfac s k]
    apply (hq k.hom).hom_ext
    · rw [Category.assoc, limit.w, hm₁, IsPullback.lift_fst]
    · rw [Category.assoc, ← limMap_π, ← Category.assoc, hm₂, IsPullback.lift_snd]

end CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

open Stacks.Groupoids

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in
-- instance search for pullbacks of presheaves on the big fppf site is slow
/-- Pullbacks of presheaves on the big fppf site over `S` (instance search times out
without this shortcut). -/
local instance hasPullbacks_presheaf_SpacesQuotientSystem :
    HasPullbacks ((BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) := inferInstance

local instance (priority := high) hasPullback_presheaf_SpacesQuotientSystem
    {X Y Z : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    HasLimit (cospan f g) :=
  HasLimitsOfShape.has_limit _

/-! ### Finite type over `Spec ℤ` from an étale chart -/

section FiniteType

/-- A chart of a presheaf on the big fppf site of `S`, read as a chart of the presheaf viewed
over `Spec ℤ`: the relocalized morphism, with its source corrected by the comparison
`Λ h_U ≅ h_{j U}` of Stacks 03I4 part (2). -/
noncomputable abbrev viewChartOverIntegers
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} (q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F) :
    yoneda.obj ((Over.map (integersMap B S hS hZ)).obj U) ⟶ viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ F :=
  ((relocalizeYonedaIso (integersMap B S hS hZ)).app U).inv ≫
    (relocalizePresheafFunctor (integersMap B S hS hZ)).map q

/-- The relocalized chart satisfies a base-change stable property `P` when the chart does. -/
private theorem presheaf_viewChartOverIntegers
    (P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) [P.IsStableUnderBaseChange]
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F}
    (hq : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage P
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage P
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)))
      (viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ q) :=
  MorphismProperty.RespectsIso.precomp _
    ((relocalizeYonedaIso (integersMap B S hS hZ)).app U).inv _
    (@presheaf_map_relocalize _ _ _ _ (integersMap B S hS hZ)
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage P (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
      (MorphismProperty.inverseImage P (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ))
      (MorphismProperty.RespectsIso.inverseImage _ _) (fun _ hk => hk) _ _ _ hq)

/-- The relocalized chart is surjective when the chart is. -/
theorem presheaf_surjective_viewChartOverIntegers
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F}
    (hq : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)))
      (viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ q) :=
  presheaf_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ _ hq

/-- The relocalized chart is étale when the chart is. -/
theorem presheaf_etale_viewChartOverIntegers
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F}
    (hq : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)))
      (viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ q) :=
  presheaf_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ _ hq

/-- **A presheaf with a quasi-compact étale chart is quasi-compact over `Spec ℤ`.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsQuasiCompactSpace` asks for a chart with quasi-compact source, and
the relocalized chart has the same underlying scheme as the given one. -/
theorem isQuasiCompactSpace_viewOverIntegers_of_chart
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F}
    (hsurj : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q)
    (hetale : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q)
    (hU : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U)) :
    IsQuasiCompactSpace B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ F) :=
  ⟨(Over.map (integersMap B S hS hZ)).obj U, viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ q, hU,
    presheaf_surjective_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ hsurj,
    isEtale_of_presheaf_etale B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
      (presheaf_etale_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ hetale)⟩

/-- The object of the big fppf site of `Spec ℤ` given by the identity of the base. -/
private noncomputable abbrev integersBase : BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ :=
  Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hZ))

/-- The presheaf it represents is terminal: the identity is a terminal object of the slice
category, and the Yoneda embedding preserves terminal objects. -/
private noncomputable def integersBaseIso :
    yoneda.obj (integersBase B hZ) ≅ ⊤_ ((BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) :=
  ((Over.mkIdTerminal (X := B.obj hZ)).isTerminalObj yoneda _).uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal

/-- **The structure morphism of a representable presheaf over `Spec ℤ` is locally of finite type
as soon as the underlying scheme is of finite type over the integers.**

The morphism to the terminal presheaf factors, by uniqueness of morphisms into a terminal
object, as the Yoneda image of the object's own structure morphism followed by the comparison
with the presheaf represented by the base, and being locally of finite type may then be
cancelled across that isomorphism and read on schemes with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFiniteType_yoneda_map_iff`. -/
theorem isLocallyOfFiniteType_terminal_yoneda
    (A : BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)
    (hA : LocallyOfFiniteType
      (terminal.from ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).obj A))) :
    IsLocallyOfFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (terminal.from (yoneda.obj A)) := by
  let h : A ⟶ integersBase B hZ := Over.homMk A.hom
  have hmap : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).map h = terminal.from _ :=
    terminal.hom_ext _ _
  have hlft : IsLocallyOfFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (yoneda.map h) :=
    (isLocallyOfFiniteType_yoneda_map_iff B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ h).2 (by rwa [hmap])
  let P : MorphismProperty ((BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) :=
    fun _ _ f => IsLocallyOfFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ f
  have _ : P.RespectsIso := isLocallyOfFiniteType_respectsIso B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
  have heq : terminal.from (yoneda.obj A) = yoneda.map h ≫ (integersBaseIso B hZ).hom :=
    terminal.hom_ext _ _
  rw [heq]
  exact (P.cancel_right_of_respectsIso (yoneda.map h) (integersBaseIso B hZ).hom).2 hlft

/-- **A presheaf with an étale chart of finite type over the integers is of finite type over
`Spec ℤ`.**  Let `F` be an algebraic space over `S` with a surjective étale chart `q` from an
object of the site whose underlying scheme is quasi-compact and locally of finite type over
the integers.  Then the view of `F` over `Spec ℤ` is of finite type over `Spec ℤ`.

Local finite type is Stacks 040Y, conditions (1) and (6), applied to the relocalized chart;
quasi-compactness of the structure morphism is Stacks 073B part (1), for which the terminal
presheaf is quasi-separated by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GluedEtaleQuotient.isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_terminal`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_of_chart
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ F}
    (hsurj : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q)
    (hetale : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) q)
    (hUqc : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hUft : LocallyOfFiniteType
      (terminal.from ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))) :
    IsFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
      (terminal.from (viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ F)) := by
  have hview : IsAlgebraicSpace B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ F) :=
    isAlgebraicSpace_relocalize B (B.obj hS) (B.obj hZ) (integersMap B S hS hZ) F hF
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · refine ((isLocallyOfFiniteType_tfae B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ hview
      (isAlgebraicSpace_terminal B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ) _).out 6 1).mp ?_
    refine ⟨(Over.map (integersMap B S hS hZ)).obj U, viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ q,
      (presheafSurjective_iff_isSurjective_yoneda B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ _ hview _ _).1
        (presheaf_surjective_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ hsurj),
      isEtale_of_presheaf_etale B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
        (presheaf_etale_viewChartOverIntegers B S hS hZ hetale), ?_⟩
    rw [terminal.comp_from]
    exact isLocallyOfFiniteType_terminal_yoneda B hZ _ hUft
  · exact isQuasiCompact_of_isQuasiCompactSpace B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ hZ
      (isAlgebraicSpace_terminal B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ)
      (GluedEtaleQuotient.isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_terminal (B := B) (hZ := hZ))
      (isQuasiCompactSpace_viewOverIntegers_of_chart B S hS hZ hsurj hetale hUqc) _

end FiniteType

/-! ### A single quotient -/

section Quotient

variable [HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)]
variable {R U : BigFppfOver B S hS} (s t : R ⟶ U)

/-- The quotient sheaf `U/R` of the étale equivalence relation determined by `s, t : R ⟶ U`,
as a presheaf on the big fppf site of `S`. -/
@[sga "3 IV 4.4.9" "special case", sga "3 VIA 3.3"]
noncomputable abbrev relationQuotient : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  (Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
    (Over.post B.inclusion) (relation B S hS s t)).obj

/-- The quotient map of Stacks 02WW is the canonical projection onto the quotient sheaf,
precomposed with the comparison between the represented presheaf and the restricted functor
of points. -/
theorem quotientMap_eq_yonedaToPoints_comp :
    quotientMap B S hS s t = yonedaToPoints (Over.post B.inclusion) U ≫
      Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
        (relation B S hS s t) :=
  yonedaEquiv_symm_app_toQuotientSheaf _ _ _ _

/-- The second kernel-pair projection of the quotient map is quasi-compact as soon as the
source morphism `s` of the relation is.

The kernel pair of the quotient map is the relation, by Stacks 02WV, so the projection differs
from `yoneda.map s` by the canonical isomorphism with the chosen pullback. -/
private theorem presheaf_quasiCompact_pullback_snd_quotientMap
    [IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation (relation B S hS s t)]
    (hs : QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map s)) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@QuasiCompact.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)))
      (pullback.snd (quotientMap B S hS s t) (quotientMap B S hS s t)) := by
  have hrespects : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@QuasiCompact.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))).RespectsIso :=
    (MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda) _).respectsIso
  have hpb := quotientMap_isPullback B S hS s t
  refine (MorphismProperty.cancel_left_of_respectsIso _ hpb.isoPullback.hom _).1 ?_
  rw [hpb.isoPullback_hom_snd]
  exact presheaf_yoneda_map_of_inverseImage B S hS (P := @QuasiCompact.{u}) inferInstance s hs

/-- **A quotient is absolutely quasi-separated when its presenting scheme is and its source
map is quasi-compact.**  Let `s, t : R ⟶ U` be an étale equivalence relation on an object of
the big fppf site of `S` whose underlying scheme is quasi-separated, and suppose the scheme
morphism underlying `s` is quasi-compact.  Then the quotient `U/R` is an absolutely
quasi-separated algebraic space over `S`.

This is Stacks 07S4 applied to the quotient map, whose kernel pair is the relation by Stacks
02WV and which is a surjective étale chart by Stacks 02WW. -/
theorem isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_quotient_of_quasiCompact_source
    [IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation (relation B S hS s t)]
    (hU : QuasiSeparatedSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hs : QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map s)) :
    IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (relationQuotient B S hS s t) :=
  isQuasiSeparated_of_etaleAtlas_quasiCompact_projection B S hS hZ _
    (isAlgebraicSpace_quotient_unconditional B S hS s t)
    ⟨U, quotientMap B S hS s t, hU,
      quotientMap_surjective_unconditional B S hS s t,
      quotientMap_etale_unconditional B S hS s t,
      Or.inr (presheaf_quasiCompact_pullback_snd_quotientMap B S hS s t hs)⟩

/-- **A quotient is of finite type over `Spec ℤ` when its presenting scheme is.**  Let
`s, t : R ⟶ U` be an étale equivalence relation on an object of the big fppf site of `S` whose
underlying scheme is quasi-compact and locally of finite type over the integers.  Then the
view of `U/R` over `Spec ℤ` is of finite type over `Spec ℤ`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_quotient
    [IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation (relation B S hS s t)]
    (hUqc : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hUft : LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))) :
    IsFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
      (terminal.from (viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ (relationQuotient B S hS s t))) :=
  isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_of_chart B S hS hZ
    (isAlgebraicSpace_quotient_unconditional B S hS s t)
    (quotientMap_surjective_unconditional B S hS s t)
    (quotientMap_etale_unconditional B S hS s t) hUqc hUft

end Quotient

/-! ### The system of quotients -/

section System

variable [HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)]
variable {J : Type*} [Preorder J] {V R : Jᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS} (s t : R ⟶ V)

omit [HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)] in
/-- The source square of a morphism of the system of relations, on the pre-relations. -/
theorem relation_source_naturality {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    (Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (R.map f) ≫
        (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j')).source =
      (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)).source ≫
        (Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (V.map f) := by
  rw [relation_source, relation_source, ← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, s.naturality]

omit [HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)] in
/-- The target square of a morphism of the system of relations, on the pre-relations. -/
theorem relation_target_naturality {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    (Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (R.map f) ≫
        (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j')).target =
      (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)).target ≫
        (Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (V.map f) := by
  rw [relation_target, relation_target, ← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, t.naturality]

/-- The transition map `V_j / R_j ⟶ V_{j'} / R_{j'}` of the system of quotients, as a morphism
of sheaves: the map of quotient sheaves induced by the morphism of relations. -/
noncomputable abbrev quotientSystemMap {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
        (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)) ⟶
      Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
        (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j')) :=
  Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
    (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)) (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j'))
    ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (R.map f)) ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (V.map f))
    (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t f) (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t f)

/-- The system of quotients as an inverse system of sheaves: `j ↦ V_j / R_j`, with the maps
of quotient sheaves induced by the morphisms of relations. -/
noncomputable def quotientSheafSystem :
    Jᵒᵖ ⥤ Sheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u) where
  obj j := Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
    (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))
  map f := quotientSystemMap B S hS s t f
  map_id j :=
    (quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (Over.post B.inclusion) (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))
      (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (R.map (𝟙 j))) (𝟙 _)
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (V.map (𝟙 j))) (𝟙 _)
      (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t (𝟙 j))
      (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t (𝟙 j))
      (by rw [Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id]) (by rw [Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id])
      (by rw [V.map_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id])).trans
      (quotientSheafMap_id (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
        (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)))
  map_comp {j₀ j₁ j₂} f g :=
    (quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (Over.post B.inclusion) (relation B S hS (s.app j₀) (t.app j₀))
      (relation B S hS (s.app j₂) (t.app j₂))
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (R.map (f ≫ g)))
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (R.map f) ≫ (Over.post B.inclusion).map (R.map g))
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (V.map (f ≫ g)))
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).map (V.map f) ≫ (Over.post B.inclusion).map (V.map g))
      (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t (f ≫ g))
      (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t (f ≫ g))
      (by rw [Category.assoc, relation_source_naturality B S hS s t g, ← Category.assoc,
            relation_source_naturality B S hS s t f, Category.assoc])
      (by rw [Category.assoc, relation_target_naturality B S hS s t g, ← Category.assoc,
            relation_target_naturality B S hS s t f, Category.assoc])
      (by rw [V.map_comp, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp])).trans
      (quotientSheafMap_comp (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Over.post B.inclusion)
        (relation B S hS (s.app j₀) (t.app j₀)) (relation B S hS (s.app j₁) (t.app j₁))
        (relation B S hS (s.app j₂) (t.app j₂)) _ _
        (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t f) (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t f)
        _ _ (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t g)
        (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t g)).symm

/-- **The system of quotients.** For a system of pairs `s, t : R ⟶ V` of morphisms of objects
of the big fppf site of `S`, the inverse system `j ↦ V_j / R_j` of quotient sheaves, with the
transition maps induced on quotient sheaves by the morphisms of relations. -/
noncomputable def relationQuotientSystem : Jᵒᵖ ⥤ (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  quotientSheafSystem B S hS s t ⋙ sheafToPresheaf _ _

/-- The stage of the system of quotients at `j` is the quotient `V_j / R_j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSystem_obj (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    (relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).obj j = relationQuotient B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j) :=
  rfl

/-- The transition maps of the system of quotients are the maps induced on quotient sheaves. -/
theorem quotientSystem_map {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    (relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).map f = (quotientSystemMap B S hS s t f).hom :=
  rfl

/-- The transition maps of the system of quotients commute with the quotient maps, read on
quotient sheaves. -/
private theorem quotientMap_comp_quotientSystemMap_hom {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    quotientMap B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j) ≫ (quotientSystemMap B S hS s t f).hom =
      yoneda.map (V.map f) ≫ quotientMap B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j') := by
  rw [quotientMap_eq_yonedaToPoints_comp, quotientMap_eq_yonedaToPoints_comp, Category.assoc,
    toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap, ← Category.assoc, yonedaToPoints_naturality,
    Category.assoc]

/-- The transition maps of the system of quotients commute with the quotient maps. -/
theorem quotientMap_comp_quotientSystem_map {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j') :
    quotientMap B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j) ≫ (relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).map f =
      yoneda.map (V.map f) ≫ quotientMap B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j') :=
  quotientMap_comp_quotientSystemMap_hom B S hS s t f

/-- **The quotient maps of the system.** The natural transformation `h_{V_j} ⟶ V_j / R_j`
whose components are the quotient maps of Stacks 02WW. -/
noncomputable def quotientSystemπ : V ⋙ yoneda ⟶ relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t where
  app j := quotientMap B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)
  naturality _ _ f := (quotientMap_comp_quotientSystem_map B S hS s t f).symm

/-- The component of `quotientSystemπ` at `j` is the quotient map `h_{V_j} ⟶ V_j / R_j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSystemπ_app (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    (quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j = quotientMap B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j) :=
  rfl

variable [∀ j, IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))]

/-- **Every stage of the system of quotients is an algebraic space** (Stacks 02WW). -/
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_quotientSystem_obj (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).obj j) :=
  isAlgebraicSpace_quotient_unconditional B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)

/-- **The quotient maps of the system are surjective** after every representable base change
(Stacks 02WW). -/
theorem quotientSystemπ_app_surjective (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j) :=
  quotientMap_surjective_unconditional B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)

/-- **The quotient maps of the system are étale** after every representable base change
(Stacks 02WW). -/
theorem quotientSystemπ_app_etale (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j) :=
  quotientMap_etale_unconditional B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)

/-- **Stacks 07S3 for the system of quotients.** When the source square of `f : j ⟶ j'` is
cartesian, so is the square formed by `V_j ⟶ V_{j'}`, the two quotient maps and the transition
map `V_j / R_j ⟶ V_{j'} / R_{j'}`.

This is `Stacks.Groupoids.isPullback_toQuotientSheaf`, transported from the restricted functors
of points to the represented presheaves along `Stacks.Groupoids.yonedaToPoints`. -/
theorem isPullback_quotientSystemπ {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j')
    (hcart : IsPullback (R.map f) (s.app j) (s.app j') (V.map f)) :
    IsPullback (yoneda.map (V.map f)) ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j)
      ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j') ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).map f) := by
  have hcart07 : IsPullback ((Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (R.map f))
      (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j)).source
      (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j')).source
      ((Over.post (X := B.obj hS) B.inclusion).map (V.map f)) := by
    rw [relation_source, relation_source]
    exact IsPullback.of_map_of_faithful (Over.forget _)
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map_isPullback hcart)
  have h07 := isPullback_toQuotientSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
    (Over.post B.inclusion) (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))
    (relation B S hS (s.app j') (t.app j')) _ _
    (relation_source_naturality B S hS s t f) (relation_target_naturality B S hS s t f) hcart07
    (BigFppfOver.isSheaf_post_inclusion_op_comp_yoneda_obj B S hS _)
    (BigFppfOver.isSheaf_post_inclusion_op_comp_yoneda_obj B S hS _)
  refine (h07.of_iso' (asIso (yonedaToPoints (Over.post B.inclusion) (V.obj j))) (Iso.refl _)
    (asIso (yonedaToPoints (Over.post B.inclusion) (V.obj j'))) (Iso.refl _)
    ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_).flip
  · exact (quotientMap_eq_yonedaToPoints_comp B S hS _ _).symm.trans (Category.comp_id _).symm
  · exact yonedaToPoints_naturality (Over.post B.inclusion) (V.map f)
  · exact (Category.id_comp _).trans (Category.comp_id _).symm
  · exact (quotientMap_eq_yonedaToPoints_comp B S hS _ _).symm.trans (Category.comp_id _).symm

/-- **The transition maps of the system of quotients are affine** when the source square of
`f` is cartesian and the scheme morphism underlying `V_j ⟶ V_{j'}` is affine.

This is Stacks 03WG, implication (4) ⇒ (2), at the surjective étale chart
`h_{V_{j'}} ⟶ V_{j'} / R_{j'}`: by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isPullback_quotientSystemπ` the
base change of the transition map along it is `h_{V_j} ⟶ h_{V_{j'}}`, which is affine by
implication (1) ⇒ (2) for represented presheaves. -/
theorem isAffineHom_quotientSystem_map {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j')
    (hcart : IsPullback (R.map f) (s.app j) (s.app j') (V.map f))
    (haff : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (V.map f))) :
    IsAffineHom B S hS ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).map f) := by
  have hX := isAlgebraicSpace_quotientSystem_obj B S hS s t
  have hrep : IsAffineHom B S hS (yoneda.map (V.map f)) :=
    ((isAffineHom_tfae_of_isAlgebraicSpace B S hS (yoneda.map (V.map f))
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _) (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _)).out 1 2).mp (by
      refine ⟨Functor.relativelyRepresentable.map yoneda _, ?_⟩
      exact presheaf_yoneda_map_of_inverseImage B S hS
        (P := @_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom.{u}) inferInstance _ haff)
  have hpb := (isPullback_quotientSystemπ B S hS s t f hcart).flip
  refine ((isAffineHom_tfae_of_isAlgebraicSpace B S hS _ (hX j) (hX j')).out 4 2).mp ?_
  refine ⟨V.obj j', (quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j',
      (presheafSurjective_iff_isSurjective_yoneda B S hS _ (hX j') _ _).1
        (quotientSystemπ_app_surjective B S hS s t j'),
      isEtale_of_presheaf_etale B S hS (quotientSystemπ_app_etale B S hS s t j'), ?_⟩
  have he : pullback.snd ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).map f)
      ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j') = hpb.isoPullback.inv ≫ yoneda.map (V.map f) := by
    rw [hpb.isoPullback_inv_snd]
  rw [he]
  exact isAffineHom_iso_comp hpb.isoPullback.inv hrep

/-- **Every stage of the system of quotients is absolutely quasi-separated** when its
presenting scheme is quasi-separated and its source map is quasi-compact (Stacks 07S4). -/
theorem isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_quotientSystem_obj (j : Jᵒᵖ)
    (hV : QuasiSeparatedSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (V.obj j)))
    (hs : QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (s.app j))) :
    IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).obj j) :=
  isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_quotient_of_quasiCompact_source B S hS hZ (s.app j) (t.app j) hV hs

/-- **Every stage of the system of quotients is of finite type over `Spec ℤ`** when its
presenting scheme is quasi-compact and locally of finite type over the integers. -/
theorem isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_quotientSystem_obj (j : Jᵒᵖ)
    (hVqc : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (V.obj j)))
    (hVft : LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (V.obj j)))) :
    IsFiniteType B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ
      (terminal.from (viewOverIntegers B S hS hZ ((relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t).obj j))) :=
  isFiniteType_viewOverIntegers_quotient B S hS hZ (s.app j) (t.app j) hVqc hVft

end System

/-- **The chart squares pass to the limit of the system of quotients.** For a directed system
of étale equivalence relations with cartesian source squares, the square formed by the
projections from the limits of `h_{V_j}` and of the quotients `V_j / R_j`, the limit of the
quotient maps and the quotient map at `j` is cartesian. -/
theorem isPullback_limit_π_limMap_quotientSystemπ
    [HasSheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type u)]
    {J : Type u} [Preorder J] [IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)] {V R : Jᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS}
    (s t : R ⟶ V) [∀ j, IsEtaleEquivalenceRelation (relation B S hS (s.app j) (t.app j))]
    (hcart : ∀ {j j' : Jᵒᵖ} (f : j ⟶ j'), IsPullback (R.map f) (s.app j) (s.app j') (V.map f))
    (j : Jᵒᵖ) :
    IsPullback (limit.π (V ⋙ yoneda) j) (limMap (quotientSystemπ B S hS s t))
      ((quotientSystemπ B S hS s t).app j) (limit.π (relationQuotientSystem B S hS s t) j) :=
  isPullback_limit_π_limMap _ (fun _ _ f => isPullback_quotientSystemπ B S hS s t f (hcart f)) j

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
